---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About | Enricco Gemha"
	description="Software engineer from São Paulo, now at Brown. iOS, backends, and the money paths between them."
>
	<div class="wrapper wrapper-narrow stack gap-12">
		<header class="intro">
			<div class="stack gap-4">
				<h1>About</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					I am a software engineer from São Paulo. I write iOS apps and the backends
					behind them, and most of what I have built ends up handling money, which is
					where the interesting problems tend to be.
				</p>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/assets/portrait.jpg"
				alt="Enricco Gemha, in a navy suit, photographed outdoors in front of evergreen trees."
				width="867"
				height="1200"
				decoding="async"
			/>
		</header>

		<section class="stack gap-3" aria-labelledby="how">
			<h2 class="section-label" id="how">How I got here</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					I started writing software in my family's medical accounting office, where
					the job was moving paper from one pile to another and the obvious fix was to
					stop doing that by hand. I taught myself Python for it, then went to Insper
					in São Paulo for computer engineering.
				</p>
				<p>
					Most of what I learned there came from things that were not coursework: two
					generations of a search-and-rescue robot that placed first in class at the
					RoboCup world championship, then running the robotics and AI club, then a
					capstone doing cloud security inside a payments company that was operating
					under PCI-DSS. I spent a summer at Stanford and a semester at Olin and
					Babson, which is how I ended up back in the United States.
				</p>
				<p>
					In 2025 I joined DAERO Group in Boston as its first engineer and built the
					iOS side of ZeroPunch, an app for construction crews. I left in July 2026 to
					start a masters at Brown, and I have been building OpenGiving since.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-3" aria-labelledby="now">
			<h2 class="section-label" id="now">What I am doing now</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					M.S. in Innovation Management and Entrepreneurship at Brown, finishing May
					2027, and taking systems security at Harvard this term. Day to day I am
					writing OpenGiving: a web app, an iOS app, an Android app and the API they
					all talk to.
				</p>
				<p>
					I am also reading my way properly into security rather than around it. My
					capstone was cloud security and my electives were cybersecurity and offensive
					tooling, but that is coursework, and coursework is not the same as having
					found something in a system nobody handed you. Closing that gap is the
					current project.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-3" aria-labelledby="tools">
			<h2 class="section-label" id="tools">Tools I reach for</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					<strong>Languages.</strong> Swift, Python, TypeScript, Go, Kotlin, C.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Building.</strong> SwiftUI and WidgetKit, FastAPI, Next.js and Astro,
					Jetpack Compose, PostgreSQL with Prisma, GraphQL.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Running it.</strong> AWS, Terraform, Railway, Vercel, GitHub Actions,
					OpenTelemetry and Grafana, Stripe Connect and PayPal.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Security.</strong> Semgrep in CI, Wazuh, ModSecurity, secret scanning
					as a required check. AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner. Working through
					CompTIA Security+.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-3" aria-labelledby="languages">
			<h2 class="section-label" id="languages">Elsewhere</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					Portuguese and English natively, Spanish well enough to work in, Swedish
					badly and improving. I have lived or studied in Brazil, the United States and
					Sweden, and you can usually find me playing pickup football somewhere.
				</p>
				<p>
					Write to me at <a href="mailto:me@enriccogemha.dev">me@enriccogemha.dev</a>,
					or find me on <a href="https://github.com/G3mha" rel="me noopener">GitHub</a>
					and <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/enriccogemha" rel="me noopener">LinkedIn</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.intro {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 2rem;
	}

	.lede {
		font-size: var(--text-lg);
		color: var(--ink);
		max-width: var(--measure);
	}

	.intro img {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 15rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	@media (min-width: 42em) {
		.intro {
			flex-direction: row;
			align-items: flex-start;
			justify-content: space-between;
			gap: 3rem;
		}

		/* The portrait stays deliberately small. It is here so a recruiter can put a
		   face to the name, not so it competes with the first paragraph. */
		.intro img {
			flex: none;
			width: 13rem;
		}
	}
</style>
